    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0130" n="118" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg118"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">648T.006/12: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-01-06T16:00:00-05:00">January 6, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. Department’s mail instruction 1134 December 26<anchor n="60" xml:id="d101-f1"
                    /> with regard to Kenya Colony regulations effective November 15, 1939, and
                    American commercial rights in that colony.</p>
                <p>The Japanese Embassy has made inquiry of us concerning this subject and we are
                    informing the Japanese Embassy that you have been instructed to bring the matter
                    appropriately to the attention of the British Government. When you make the
                    approach to British officials contemplated in the final paragraph of the
                    Department’s instruction of December 26 the Department suggests that you inform
                    those officials orally of the Japanese approach to us and of our reply.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
